    "description": "Apple II 早期配套的模拟摇杆外设，经游戏端口接入主机，提供双轴方向与动作键输入。",
    "intro": {
      "zh": "Apple II 游戏摇杆是苹果 II 个人电脑早期的游戏输入外设，与主机板载的游戏端口配合使用。它没有独立的处理器与固件，主体是安装在底座上的可摆动摇杆与动作按键：摇杆通过双轴电位器输出随偏转方向与幅度变化的模拟量，按键输出开关量，信号沿线缆送入 Apple II 的 game_port。作为一台纯输入外设，它不产生任何显示、声音或打印输出，也不携带 ROM、固件或任何存储介质。在箱庭电子博物馆中，它作为 Apple II 游戏生态的代表性外设，以静态展示配合摇杆摆动、按键按压演示呈现。",
      "en": "The Apple II game joystick is an early analog input peripheral for the Apple II personal computer, used with the computer's onboard game port. It has no processor or firmware of its own; its body is a base with a deflectable stick and action buttons. The stick outputs analog values that vary with direction and magnitude through two-axis potentiometers, while the buttons output switch signals, all carried over a cable into the Apple II game port. As a pure input peripheral it produces no display, audio or print output and carries no ROM, firmware or storage media. In the Hako Electronic Museum it represents the game ecosystem of the Apple II and is shown as a static exhibit with stick-swing and button-press demonstrations."
    },
